{"state": {"passage": "A studio audience is an audience present for the filming of all or part of a television program, or to a smaller extent, radio programs. The primary purpose of the studio audience is to provide applause and/or laughter to the program's soundtrack (as opposed to canned laughter). Additionally, live studio audiences produce an energy from which the actors can feed off, as well as push them to perform to the best of their abilities. Unlike relying on the ideal chuckles that a laugh track consistently provides, actors have to work for the laughs. A studio audience can also provide volunteers, a visual backdrop and discussion participants. On some game shows, contestants are taken from the studio audience, such as with The Price Is Right.", "question": "are any shows still filmed in front of a live studio audience"}, "questions": {"answer": {"type": "noul", "instructions": "Based on `passage`, is the answer to `question` yes?"}}, "expected": {"answer": true}, "tags": ["boolq", "id:5386", "t3arm:dev"], "language": "en"}
